# Line endings are LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# Git's default on Windows is to convert text files to CRLF on checkout, and this
# tree cannot take that.  A .result file is compared byte for byte against what the
# server wrote, so a CRLF copy differs on every line of every test; mysqltest reads
# .test and .inc files a line at a time and a trailing \r becomes part of the last
# argument on the line; and mtr's own parsers reject a "blank" line that carries a
# lone \r.  None of it fails loudly enough to be obvious -- it reads as the engine
# being broken on Windows.
#
# Declaring it here rather than relying on each contributor's core.autocrlf is what
# makes a Windows clone identical to a Linux one without anyone configuring anything.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
